<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16278" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσκ-ητός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>curiously wrought,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					4.134
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					23.189
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρίματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Xenoph.
					3.6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἵματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					24.140
				</span></i>
			; <i>adorned, decked,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέπλῳ</span>
			<i>with</i> . . , <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				1.33
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.219.3
			</span></i> (Antip.). Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τῶς</span> prob.l. in <i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				157
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to be got</i> or <i>reached by practice,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ διδακτὸν ἀλλ᾽ ἀ.,</span> of virtue,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Men.</u>
				70a
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				1.2.23
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαθητὸν ἢ ἐθιστὸν ἢ καὶ ἄλλως πως
					ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1099b10
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of persons,
				<i>exercised, practised in</i> a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀθηναίης παλάμῃσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
				</span></i>
			 l. c. (codd. <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνὴρ ἀ. καὶ σοφός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Lyc.</u>
					30
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
